An explicitly named directory is walked even when ignored, and git semantics keep ancestor rules for it.
== args
repo/dist
== file repo/.git/HEAD
ref: refs/heads/main
== file repo/.gitignore
dist/
*.map.md
== file repo/dist/bundle.md
---
description: Explicitly requested, so walked.
---
# bundle
== file repo/dist/bundle.map.md
---
description: Ignored by the ancestor *.map.md rule, which still applies inside an ignored root.
---
# map
== file repo/dist/.gitignore
skip.md
== file repo/dist/skip.md
---
description: Ignored by the root's own .gitignore.
---
# skip
== stdout
glob view: repo/dist
repo/dist/bundle.md (4 lines): description: "Explicitly requested, so walked."
